    {
      "text": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium, indirect heat and lightly oil the grate.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Season pork tenderloins with garlic powder, salt, and pepper. Place 1/2 of the BBQ sauce into a small bowl for basting; set aside remaining BBQ sauce for serving.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/x1jyL0aCfvW7HXF8HY1Q_LbvQB4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14726-grilled-pork-tenderloin-step-02-67368ad686a84a6fb7af47f70120d909.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14726/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook pork on the preheated grill over indirect heat for 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/12VHO0m--_jg1u_g-jeH18BZw1w=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14726-grilled-pork-tenderloin-step-04-854fe14b08c64bfca7e3db0d72ee9b5b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14726/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Brush pork with BBQ sauce, turn, and brush again, using all sauce in the small bowl. Continue cooking until an instant-read thermometer inserted into the center reads 145 degrees F (63 degrees C), about 15 more minutes. Let pork rest for 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/9eJnbMJ5rDhwFbaz2iffc0LYf2A=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14726-grilled-pork-tenderloin-step-06-3d047c59eb0a4dd5adad17881cdfd2b0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14726/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice pork and serve with reserved BBQ sauce.",
